from pathlib import Path
import json,html
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((R/'SUMMARY.json').read_text())
def esc(x):return html.escape(str(x))
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(x)+'</td>' for x in [r['volume'],r['scenario'],round(r['medianW'],1),str(r['admitted'])+'/100',str(r['flags'])+'/'+str(r['admitted']),r['diagnostic_flags'],', '.join(f'{v:.3f}' for v in r['wilson95']),r['status']])+'</tr>' for r in s['results'])
doc='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Shift-tolerant sh/qok qualification</title><style>body{font:17px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1180px;margin:35px auto;padding:24px;background:#f8faf7;color:#193b31}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}td,th{padding:9px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #c5d4c9} .table{overflow:auto}a{color:#165f89}code{background:#e9efeb}</style><h1>Can relative position recover usable comparisons?</h1><p><strong>Frozen candidate status: '''+esc(s['status'])+'''</strong>. Synthetic controls only; no manuscript files loaded or scored. H/F remain separate and untouched.</p><p>Revision: use the first nonoverlapping same-body pair in each line; group by page, body, relative-position thirds and follower availability. Preserve the sh/ch composition of each retained line and orientation totals within each group. Exact length and exact absolute position are deliberately relaxed.</p><p>All samples vary front and back padding, replace 20% of target origins, and retain 5% unknown-token slots. Volume 1 uses the original active-line budget; volume 4 supplies four times as many active lines, keeping the blocked-line count fixed. It is a separate larger-sample test, not evidence that the original sample has adequate power.</p><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Volume</th><th>Control</th><th>Median W</th><th>Admitted</th><th>Flags / admitted</th><th>Flags / all 100</th><th>Admitted Wilson 95%</th><th>Gate</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table></div><h2>What the controls ask</h2><p><code>null_low</code> and <code>null_high</code> use independent follower choices. <code>null_layout</code> makes both prefix placement and follower choices respond to a smooth relative-position trend. <code>null_nonlinear</code> adds oscillating position effects and absolute-position parity. Neither layout null uses the preceding prefix to generate followers. A significant result there mistakes shared layout for the targeted association beyond layout.</p><p>The positive control adds 15 percentage points to qok probability after sh among structurally available followers (20% versus 35%). The correction remains eightfold. The frozen support rule is W ≥ 160, at least eight contributing pages, and no page above 25% of support. These thresholds are candidate rules under the revised matching, not inherited proof.</p><h2>Qualification and preserved failures</h2><p>Each cell requires at least 80 of 100 layouts admitted. Null false-positive Wilson upper bounds must be ≤10%; positive conditional and all-attempt power lower bounds must be ≥80%. Every cell must pass. Unsupported cells are retained, with diagnostic scores shown separately; they are not negative evidence about a manuscript effect.</p><p>Raw token roundtrips, unknown slots, outcome-invariant grouping/support, and a small exhaustive subset-distribution oracle are checked. The convolution uses floating-point normalized probabilities of exact combinatorial subset distributions, not Monte Carlo permutations. Availability is known from the synthetic construction; inferring availability from real writing remains a separate unqualified step.</p><p>These are authored stress tests, not estimates of the manuscript's nuisance strengths. Coarse thirds are one candidate, not all possible shift-tolerant methods. No grammar or semantic claim follows.</p><p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Hashes</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.json">Summary and intervals</a> · <a href="TRIALS.json">All attempts, including failures</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Checks</a> · <a href="run.py">Reproducible generator and test</a></p></html>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(doc,encoding='utf-8')
for f in ['PROTOCOL.json','FREEZE.json','SUMMARY.json','TRIALS.json','VERIFICATION.json','run.py']:assert (R/f).exists()
print(json.dumps(s,indent=2))
